{
  "title": "Images in Next.js",
  "date": "2020-11-11",
  "tags": [
    "next js",
    "guide"
  ],
  "draft": false,
  "summary": "In this article we introduce adding images in the tailwind starter blog and the benefits and limitations of the next/image component.",
  "authors": [
    "sparrowhawk"
  ],
  "portableTextBody": [
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h1",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Introduction",
          "_key": "ibkpmv"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The tailwind starter blog has out of the box support for ",
          "_key": "62bmsi"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "es8ic2"
          ],
          "text": "Next.js's built-in image component",
          "_key": "rf9ct1"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and automatically swaps out default image tags in markdown or mdx documents to use the Image component provided.",
          "_key": "hxfm0j"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_type": "link",
          "_key": "es8ic2",
          "href": "https://nextjs.org/docs/api-reference/next/image"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h1",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Usage",
          "_key": "sgo6vu"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To use in a new page route / javascript file, simply import the image component and call it e.g.",
          "_key": "aux9m9"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "code",
      "language": "js",
      "code": "import Image from 'next/image'\n\nfunction Home() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <h1>My Homepage</h1>\n      <Image src=\"/me.png\" alt=\"Picture of the author\" width={500} height={500} />\n      <p>Welcome to my homepage!</p>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\nexport default Home"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a markdown file, the default image tag can be used and the default ",
          "_key": "ngsfvo"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "img",
          "_key": "mjr8fd"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " tag gets replaced by the ",
          "_key": "1j2i3t"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "Image",
          "_key": "sg1vd0"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " component in the build process.",
          "_key": "ptk521"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Assuming we have a file called ",
          "_key": "c88eqh"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "ocean.jpg",
          "_key": "o8ugq2"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " in ",
          "_key": "6l6p9m"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "static/images/ocean.jpg",
          "_key": "sfwzce"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", the following line of code would generate the optimized image.",
          "_key": "cq2sqf"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "code",
      "language": null,
      "code": "![ocean](/static/images/ocean.jpg)"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Alternatively, since we are using mdx, we can just use the image component directly! Note, that you would have to provide a fixed width and height. The ",
          "_key": "ynbgx5"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "img",
          "_key": "2txxct"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " tag method parses the dimension automatically.",
          "_key": "d96yo9"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "code",
      "language": "js",
      "code": "<Image alt=\"ocean\" src=\"/static/images/ocean.jpg\" width={256} height={128} />"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "em"
          ],
          "text": "Note",
          "_key": "0wp1g9"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ": If you try to save the image, it is in webp format, if your browser supports it!",
          "_key": "apsy5m"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "[Image: ocean]",
          "_key": "8kjzpt"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Photo by ",
          "_key": "nlo0jt"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "wwztfg"
          ],
          "text": "YUCAR FotoGrafik",
          "_key": "wttzg3"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\non ",
          "_key": "nqoj1n"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "fe9cet"
          ],
          "text": "Unsplash",
          "_key": "48ynrf"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_type": "link",
          "_key": "wwztfg",
          "href": "https://unsplash.com/@yucar?utm_source=unsplash&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=creditCopyText"
        },
        {
          "_type": "link",
          "_key": "fe9cet",
          "href": "https://unsplash.com/s/photos/sea?utm_source=unsplash&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=creditCopyText"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h1",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Benefits",
          "_key": "rewl4j"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Smaller image size with Webp (~30% smaller than jpeg)",
          "_key": "c3ryw9"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Responsive images - the correct image size is served based on the user's viewport",
          "_key": "rg7gyj"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Lazy loading - images load as they are scrolled to the viewport",
          "_key": "w8d07x"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Avoids ",
          "_key": "064vlk"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "0otonu"
          ],
          "text": "Cumulative Layout Shift",
          "_key": "dyd4ln"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_type": "link",
          "_key": "0otonu",
          "href": "https://web.dev/cls/"
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Optimization on demand instead of build-time - no increase in build time!",
          "_key": "92ybci"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h1",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Limitations",
          "_key": "x0p8pr"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Due to the reliance on ",
          "_key": "eyiobg"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "next/image",
          "_key": "9l8keb"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", unless you are using an external image CDN like Cloudinary or Imgix, it is practically required to use Vercel for hosting. This is because the component acts like a serverless function that calls a highly optimized image CDN.",
          "_key": "aic9b5"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If you do not want to be tied to Vercel, you can remove ",
          "_key": "ubdu2r"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "imgToJsx",
          "_key": "b7lxbx"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " in ",
          "_key": "pm9d4o"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "remarkPlugins",
          "_key": "k8cmjk"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " in ",
          "_key": "6nllnb"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "lib/mdx.js",
          "_key": "woliit"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". This would avoid substituting the default ",
          "_key": "ha2b8j"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "img",
          "_key": "h1qvpq"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " tag.",
          "_key": "uhh16f"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Alternatively, one could wait for image optimization at build time to be supported. A different library, ",
          "_key": "fyhd3l"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "o07n8v"
          ],
          "text": "next-optimized-images",
          "_key": "3xl4ew"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " does that, although it requires transforming the images through webpack which is not done here.",
          "_key": "llktad"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_type": "link",
          "_key": "o07n8v",
          "href": "https://github.com/cyrilwanner/next-optimized-images"
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Images from external links are not passed through ",
          "_key": "ionj8q"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "next/image",
          "_key": "q87ib2"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "All images have to be stored in the ",
          "_key": "6k5r0i"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "public",
          "_key": "t8f9fg"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " folder e.g ",
          "_key": "4yjxjq"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "/static/images/ocean.jpeg",
          "_key": "6xgb07"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    }
  ]
}